== Points of Interest ==
=== Name Rater ===
In the tent, the player will find the Name Rater. If shown a Pokémon with a "perfect nickname", he will give the player a {{ItemIcon|machine_NORMAL}} TM87 Swagger.

''Inspecting the picture next to the Name Rater gives a hint on what is a perfect nickname.''

A Name Rater considers a perfect nickname to be both starting with the same letter and ending with the same letter as the Pokémon's species.

=== Hidden Tomb ===
[[File:QuestTime_LavenderTown.png|thumb|255x249px]]
By ringing the bell next to the Pokémon Tower at the right time, the entrance to the Hidden Tomb will appear.

The objective for the "For Whom the Bell Tolls" [[Quests|quest]] started in [[Celadon City|Celadon City's]] hotel is to solve the riddle to open the Hidden Tomb. 

{{Quote|...the bell in Lavender Town reveal its secret if one rings it at night, when the time is right.}}

''The tomb can be opened without starting the quest however due to a bug, the quest cannot be completed if the tomb had already been opened.''
{{Clear}}
=== Ominous Wind Move Tutor ===
A girl in the western house will teach [[bulbapedia:Ominous Wind (move)|Ominous Wind]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}2,500.

=== Morty Rematch ===
After clearing [[Mt. Silver]], Morty can be found next to the Pokémon Tower during the [[Time|night]]. After talking to him, he will appear at the Fighting Arena in [[Vermillion City]] for a [[Gym Leader rematches|rematch]].

